\begin{center}
{\Large\itshape\color{CoverGoldBright} וַיְמַן יְהוָה}\\[0.1cm]
{\itshape\small\color{CoverMuted} {\baskervillefont "And the LORD appointed"} · 全書四次「安排」(1:17；4:6、7、8)}

\vspace{0.4cm}

\fleuron[CoverGoldBright]\hspace{0.25cm}{\color{CoverGoldBright}\rule{1.8in}{0.4pt}}\hspace{0.25cm}\fleuron[CoverGoldBright]

\vspace{0.4cm}

{\large\bfseries\color{CoverCream} 關於本書}\qquad{\baskervillefont\itshape\large\color{CoverGoldBright} About This Book}

\vspace{0.4cm}

\begin{minipage}{5in}
\small\color{CoverCream}
約拿書只有四章四十八節，卻從頭到尾由神的動作推進：話兩次臨到一個逃跑的先知，風、籤、魚、蓖麻、蟲、東風，一件一件被「安排」；最後一句不是約拿的回答，是神的問題。本書分四步逐節研讀全卷，以「啟示的次序」為骨幹，整合老弟兄的查經方法、奧古斯丁、加爾文與亨利的歷代注疏，以及 G. Campbell Morgan 的解經。每一句歸給注疏家的引文都附英文原文與出處，可以按圖索驥核對。

\vspace{0.3cm}

{\baskervillefont\color{CoverCream}\lettrine[lines=3,findent=2pt,nindent=2pt]{\color{CoverGoldBright}J}{}onah has four chapters and forty-eight verses, and almost everything in it is done by God: His word comes twice to a prophet who runs, and a wind, a lot, a fish, a plant, a worm and an east wind are each “appointed” in turn. The book does not end with Jonah's answer; it ends with God's question. This study reads the whole book in four movements, built on the order of revelation, with Elder Wong's way of reading Scripture, the commentary of Augustine, John Calvin and Matthew Henry, and G. Campbell Morgan's exposition. Every quotation attributed to a commentator is given in its original English with a source a reader can check.}
\end{minipage}

\vspace{0.4cm}

{\small\bfseries\color{CoverCream} 四步：從被差遣到被詢問}\qquad{\baskervillefont\itshape\small\color{CoverGoldBright} Four Movements}

\vspace{0.3cm}

\begin{minipage}{4.7in}
\small\color{CoverCream}
\begin{tabular}{@{}cp{3.4in}l@{}}
第一步 & 神先開口，也先動手 \textit{\baskervillefont\color{CoverCream} The word comes, the wind comes} & {\tiny\color{CoverMuted} 1:1-16}\\[0.25em]
第二步 & 安排在先，禱告在後 \textit{\baskervillefont\color{CoverCream} Appointed first, prayed after} & {\tiny\color{CoverMuted} 1:17-2:10}\\[0.25em]
第三步 & 話二次臨到，神也後悔 \textit{\baskervillefont\color{CoverCream} The second time, and God relents} & {\tiny\color{CoverMuted} 3:1-10}\\[0.25em]
第四步 & 神以問題收尾 \textit{\baskervillefont\color{CoverCream} God ends with a question} & {\tiny\color{CoverMuted} 4:1-11}\\
\end{tabular}
\end{minipage}

\vspace{0.4cm}

{\color{CoverGoldBright}\rule{2.3in}{0.6pt}}

\vspace{0.25cm}

{\normalsize\itshape\color{CoverCream} 何況這尼尼微大城，其中不能分辨左手右手的有十二萬多人，\\並有許多牲畜，我豈能不愛惜呢？}\\
{\baskervillefont\footnotesize\itshape\color{CoverMuted} "Should I not have compassion on Nineveh, the great city . . . as well as many animals?" — Jonah 4:11}

